  "articleBodyHtml": "<h2>Character&#x27;s Admission of Failure</h2>\n<p>The character acknowledges her failure, as indicated by phrases like &#x27;Ah, whoops&#x27; and &#x27;It&#x27;s okay, sometimes, you know.&#x27; This suggests a moment of self-awareness and acceptance of her mistakes.</p>\n<h2>Affection for the Flower</h2>\n<p>There is evidence that the character cares for the flower, as seen in her statements such as &#x27;Your flower&#x27; and &#x27;It&#x27;s the only flower.&#x27; This implies a personal connection to the flower.</p>\n<h2>Realization of Ownership</h2>\n<p>The character realizes that the flower is not hers, as she says, &#x27;It&#x27;s not my flower.&#x27; This indicates a moment of clarity regarding the flower&#x27;s true ownership.</p>\n<h2>Confusion and Attempt to Resolve It</h2>\n<p>The character appears confused, as shown by her reaction &#x27;Huh?&#x27; and her attempt to make sense of the situation with &#x27;Because in the end.&#x27; However, she is also trying to move past this confusion, as seen in her statement &#x27;I have my flower.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Justification of Actions</h2>\n<p>The character is attempting to justify her actions, as seen in her statement &#x27;I&#x27;ve been trying to be kind all along.&#x27; This suggests she is trying to make sense of her behavior or defend it.</p>\n<h2>Use of Humor</h2>\n<p>The character uses humor to defuse the situation, as seen in her repeated line &#x27;I have it in my hand&#x27; and &#x27;No, this is your flower, no.&#x27; This indicates an attempt to lighten the mood.</p>\n<h2>Intrusion and Dismissal</h2>\n<p>There is an indication of someone breaking into the room to check on the speaker&#x27;s safety and snoop through their belongings, as suggested by the dialogue &#x27;Breaking and entering?&#x27; and &#x27;Snooping through my stuff?&#x27; The speaker, however, dismisses this as a harmless prank, as seen in the line &#x27;I&#x27;m just messing with you, Lady Bloodbrain.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Demand for Return of Records</h2>\n<p>The speaker is demanding the return of expensive records that were left in a specific location, as seen in the dialogue &#x27;What did you do with my records?&#x27; and &#x27;They were quite expensive, you know, so I would like them back.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Location of Records and Surroundings</h2>\n<p>The speaker indicates that the records are present and describes the surrounding buildings, as seen in the line &#x27;It&#x27;s all here.&#x27; and &#x27;Wow, these are very nice buildings.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Discussion of Figurines</h2>\n<p>The speaker is discussing another person&#x27;s collection of figurines and expresses frustration about their own inability to obtain them, as seen in the dialogue &#x27;How did she get so many figures now?&#x27; and &#x27;Ugh, I&#x27;m just trying to get some figurines, oh, not for them.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Request for Help with Figurine</h2>\n<p>The speaker is attempting to obtain a figurine from a &#x27;surprise box&#x27; and asks for assistance, revealing they possess &#x27;stained souls,&#x27; as seen in the dialogue &#x27;I&#x27;m trying to get a figurine from the surprise box, but I don&#x27;t, I, they&#x27;re hard to come by.&#x27; and &#x27;I have some stained souls, I will...&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Discussion of Relationship</h2>\n<p>The character is discussing her relationship with the speaker, as seen in the dialogue &#x27;I was so fine with you.&#x27; and &#x27;A message.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Confusion About Queen&#x27;s Conversation</h2>\n<p>The character is confused about the queen&#x27;s conversation with the speaker, as seen in the dialogue &#x27;I don&#x27;t know what the queen will talk to you.&#x27; and &#x27;What?&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Description of Food</h2>\n<p>The food is described as seasoned, crispy on the outside, and a little bit spicy, as seen in the dialogue &#x27;Seasoned, a little bit crispy on the outside&#x27; and &#x27;Oh yeah, it&#x27;s a little bit spicy, yeah.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Expression of Hunger and Encouragement to Eat</h2>\n<p>The speaker is hungry and is encouraging someone to eat, as seen in the dialogue &#x27;I&#x27;m hungry!&#x27; and &#x27;Please eat up!&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Instruction to Make Something</h2>\n<p>Someone is instructing others to make something, as seen in the dialogue &#x27;You know how to make them&#x27; and &#x27;I will protect your purity and save you forever.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Offer of Protection and Salvation</h2>\n<p>A character offers protection and a promise of eternal salvation, as seen in the dialogue &#x27;I will protect your purity and save you forever.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Instruction to Stop</h2>\n<p>Someone instructs others to stop, as seen in the dialogue &#x27;That&#x27;s enough.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Denial of Relationship</h2>\n<p>A character denies a relationship, as seen in the dialogue &#x27;You&#x27;re not my baby.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Offer of Protection</h2>\n<p>A character offers protection to another, as seen in the dialogue &#x27;I will protect him if you want.&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Acknowledgement of Statement</h2>\n<p>There is an acknowledgment of a statement, as seen in the dialogue &#x27;Okay!&#x27;</p>\n<h2>Repetition of Name &#x27;Jonathan&#x27;</h2>\n<p>Characters repeatedly call out &#x27;Jonathan,&#x27; as seen in the dialogue &#x27;Jonathan!&#x27;, &#x27;Jonathan!&#x27;, and &#x27;Jonathan!&#x27;</p>\n<h2>記事情報</h2>\n<p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eKVBp9EgDLc</p>",
